; +-----------------------------------------+
; The default gold rules on USDJPY (USDJPYm, 3 decimals), meant to run NEXT TO gold on the same account.
; EXPERIMENTAL - backtested only; demo forward-test before using real money. Attach it to an M5 chart.
; Not tuned: every distance is gold's, scaled by USDJPY's daily volatility (median D1 ATR, 2022-2026):
;   Stop / checkpoint : 786 points = 0.786 yen (gold: $20), entry spacing 393 points (half of it).
;   D1 trend filter   : close at least 0.309% beyond the EMA50 (gold: 0.5%).
;   Spread cap        : 20 points (2 pips).
;   PointInputDigits=0 (points are USDJPY's own), MaxLotSize 0.20 (about $100 at the stop, like gold's 0.05).
;   DrawdownScope = This EA's Own Trades: gold's losses don't raise this chart's entry score (and back).
; Backtest v50.0, M5, $2,000 per month (each month a fresh run), 1.25% risk sizing, sums of monthly returns:
;   2022 +54.6% / 2023 +0.8% / 2024 +43.8% / 2025 -9.7% / Jan-Sep 2026 -7.8%
;   57 months: +81.6%, 26/57 months up, worst month -6.9%; monthly correlation with the gold EA -0.18.
;   USDJPY makes its money in its own big trends (2022, 2024) - often when gold goes sideways.
; Gold (default.set) + this profile on one account, both at 1.25% risk (sum of the monthly runs):
;   +211.3% vs gold alone +129.7%, drawdown across months 30.4% vs 28.2%, 2022 +42.9% vs -11.6%.
; Requirements / warnings:
;   - Same hedging account as gold; on the gold chart set DrawdownScope = This EA's Own Trades too.
;   - With both running, up to 4 positions and about 5% of equity can be at risk at the same time.
;   - Alone, USDJPY is a weak earner (lost in 2025 and 2026): use it as gold's partner, not instead.
; +-----------------------------------------+
